{"acceptance_length": 2.4134615384615383, "acceptance_lengths": [2, 3, 1, 1, 4, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 4, 4, 5, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 4, 3, 1, 2, 4, 1, 1, 1, 5, 1, 1, 1, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 5, 1, 1, 1, 2, 3, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 6, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 2, 1, 1, 4, 2, 6, 4, 2, 8, 2, 2, 1, 5, 6, 1, 2, 1, 3, 7, 1, 1, 2, 1, 4, 4, 5, 2, 2, 4, 1, 6, 10, 5, 1, 1, 6, 6, 1, 1, 3, 3, 1, 1], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 34409765888, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 34409763328, "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "To find the number of positive whole-number divisors of 196, we need to find its prime factorization.\n\nStep 1: Find the prime factorization of 196.\n196 can be divided by 2 (its smallest prime factor), so we start by dividing it by 2:\n196 \u00f7 2 = 98\n98 can also be divided by 2:\n98 \u00f7 2 = 49\n49 can be divided by 7 (since 49 is 7^2):\n49 \u00f7 7 = 7\nNow we have the prime factorization of 196:\n196 = 2^2 * 7^2\n\nStep 2: Use the prime factorization to find the number of divisors.\nThe formula to find the number of divisors of a number is to add 1 to each exponent in the prime factorization and then multiply these numbers together. In this case, the exponents are 2 and 2, so we add 1 to each:\n(2 + 1) * (2 + 1) = 3 * 3 = 9\n\nTherefore, the number of positive whole-number divisors of 196 is 9.\n\n\\boxed{9}", "decode_seconds": 6.218731150962412, "draft_calls": 104, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 62, "method": "relay_p_cross_family", "output_hash": "94a6296073136f79334d99441e12dfda9adcceef0e57f59ef9541f580d56569d", "output_token_ids": [1271, 1505, 279, 1396, 315, 6928, 4459, 26939, 3512, 42314, 315, 220, 5162, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1505, 1202, 10461, 8331, 2065, 382, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 7531, 279, 10461, 8331, 2065, 315, 220, 5162, 627, 5162, 649, 387, 18255, 555, 220, 17, 320, 1220, 25655, 10461, 8331, 705, 779, 584, 1212, 555, 50802, 433, 555, 220, 17, 512, 5162, 1717, 115, 220, 17, 284, 220, 3264, 198, 3264, 649, 1101, 387, 18255, 555, 220, 17, 5